<title>SINGAPORE: INDIA OFFERS AUG/SEPT BOMBAY HAN NAPHTHA BY TENDER.</title>
<headline>INDIA OFFERS AUG/SEPT BOMBAY HAN NAPHTHA BY TENDER.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-08-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>State-owned Indian Oil Corp (IOC) has issued a tender to sell 25,000 tonnes of high aromatic naphtha (HAN) lifting from Bombay on the west coast between August 31-September 2, industry sources said on Monday.</p>
<p>The tender closes August 13 and is valid for a day.</p>
<p>IOC's last Bombay HAN cargo, lifting August 3-5, was awarded to Dutch trader Vitol at around $28 per tonne below U.S. Gulf Coast 87-octane gasoline quotes on a free-on-board (fob) basis, traders said.</p>
